    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/alma/jobs/5547347/advertising-digital-marketing-coordinator": {
      "title": "Advertising & Digital Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Advertising & Digital Marketing Coordinator Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Alma Job Type Staff - Full-Time Job Number 2026-00053 Division Enrollment Department Communication & Marketing Opening Date 11/11/2026 Closing Date 12/4/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Description Benefits POSITION SUMMARY The Advertising & Digital Marketing Coordinator develops, executes, and optimizes Alma College's advertising strategy to support enrollment, graduate programs, institutional priorities, and brand awareness. Working closely with the Senior Director of Marketing, the coordinator plans and manages paid media campaigns across digital, social, search, print, outdoor, and emerging channels. The coordinator serves as the College's primary expert on media planning and advertising performance, recommending audience strategies, media placements, budgets, and campaign investments that advance institutional goals. This position manages relationships with media partners, advertising agencies, digital platforms, and vendors while ensuring marketing resources are used effectively and responsibly. The Advertising & Digital Marketing Coordinator collaborates with admissions, graduate programs, advancement, athletics, and campus partners to develop integrated campaigns that generate awareness, engagement, inquiries, applications, and enrollment. The coordinator will work collaboratively with other members of the marketing team to maximize College resources. The coordinator will collaborate with media organizations to secure and place media. Supervision Received/Exercised This position reports to the senior director of marketing and has no supervisory responsibilities. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Develop and implement comprehensive advertising strategies that support student recruitment, graduate enrollment, fundraising, brand awareness, and other institutional priorities. Plan, execute, and optimize paid digital campaigns across Google Ads, Microsoft Advertising (Bing/MSN), Meta (Facebook and Instagram), LinkedIn, YouTube, display networks, and other platforms. Research target audiences and recommend appropriate media strategies, channel selections, audience segmentation, and campaign tactics. Manage all aspects of media planning and buying, including digital, print, billboard, streaming, broadcast, outdoor, and emerging media opportunities. Negotiate advertising rates, placements, contracts, value-added opportunities, and schedules with media organizations and vendors. Serve as the primary liaison to advertising agencies, media groups, publishers, billboard vendors, and digital platform representatives. Monitor campaign performance and analyze key metrics including reach, impressions, engagement, click-through rates, conversions, cost-per-lead, cost-per-acquisition, and return on investment. Develop dashboards, reports, and recommendations that translate campaign data into actionable marketing decisions. Manage advertising budgets, purchase orders, contracts, invoices, reconciliations, and vendor payments while ensuring compliance with College purchasing procedures. Collaborate with designers, writers, photographers, videographers, and marketing colleagues to develop compelling advertising creative and messaging. Support enrollment and marketing leadership in evaluating new advertising technologies, platforms, audience opportunities, and media trends. Conduct market and competitor research to identify opportunities and improve campaign performance. Ensure campaigns align with Alma College brand standards and institutional messaging. Other duties as assigned. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in marketing, advertising, communications, digital media, business, public relations, or a related field. Two or more years of professional experience in advertising, digital marketing, media buying, communications, or a related area. Demonstrated experience managing paid advertising campaigns across Google, Microsoft Advertising (Bing/MSN), Meta, LinkedIn, YouTube, and similar platforms. Experience developing and managing multi-channel advertising and lead generation strategies. Knowledge of audience targeting, campaign optimization, conversion tracking, attribution, and digital marketing analytics. Experience using Google Analytics and other marketing reporting tools. Experience managing advertising budgets and monitoring campaign performance against financial goals. Experience reviewing and processing invoices, purchase orders, contracts, and vendor agreements. Strong project management, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to interpret data and make evidence-based recommendations. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously. Ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, media partners, agencies, and vendors PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working directly with billboard companies, media groups, publishers, and advertising agencies. Experience in higher education marketing, enrollment marketing, or mission-driven organizations. Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta, or related digital marketing certifications. Experience working with underrepresented, first-generation, Pell-eligible, and diverse populations. Alma College is classified as a selective Baccalaureate College: Diverse Fields by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. Alma is committed to academic excellence and the development of responsible leaders; our students thrive on challenging academic programs in a supportive, small-college environment emphasizing active, collaborative learning and close student-faculty interaction. Alma is a private Phi Beta Kappa institution located in the center of Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. Alma College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse faculty, staff, and student body. Alma College recognizes that we are all transformed when we celebrate and value the varied identities, backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives in our campus community. We are committed to recognizing and removing barriers to success and providing equitable access to opportunities through education and advocacy. In our increasingly diverse campus and world, we pledge to create a climate where everyone is safe and free to grow intellectually, spiritually, and emotionally. We offer a comprehensive benefits package to employees in eligible positions working 30 hours or more per week. Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plans; flexible spending accounts; life insurance; long-term disability; paid holidays; vacation; and sick leave. Part-time employees who average 20 hours per week over the course of a year are eligible for select benefits on a prorated basis. For additional details, please visit our Prospective Employees page. Employer Alma College (MI) Address 614 W. Superior St. Alma, Michigan, 48801 Phone 989-463-7467 Website https://www.alma.edu Apply"
    }
